Available agent types for the Agent tool:
- architectural-reviewer: System-level architectural reviewer. Analyzes module boundaries, dependency graph, SOLID compliance, data flow, dependency health (§X governance), long-term maintainability, and system-level security across the full codebase. Reports findings with concrete fix options. Does NOT modify code. Automatically persists output with actionable todo checklist. (Tools: Bash, Read, Glob, Grep, Write, LSP)
- claude: Catch-all for any task that doesn't fit a more specific agent. FleetView's default when no agent name is typed. (Tools: *)
- dependency-researcher: Evaluates npm package candidates for the Dependency Governance protocol (COMMON.md §IX). Researches alternatives, compares bundle size, license, maintenance, and security. Returns a structured recommendation. Does NOT install packages or write code. (Tools: Read, Glob, Grep, WebSearch, WebFetch)
- dp-python-analyze-extractor: Scans a Python/Odoo project and produces a structured intermediate representation (IR) in claude-artifacts/python-analysis/ir/. Extracts modules, classes, functions, imports, dependencies, and Odoo-specific artifacts. Uses LSP (Pyright) when available, Grep fallback otherwise. (Tools: Bash, Read, Write, Glob, Grep, LSP)
- dp-qg-attribute: Attribution resolver for needs-judgment findings. Receives findings the deterministic classifier could not resolve, reads spec/plan/rules/diff context, and classifies each to one of {rule-induced, rule-missed, runner-defect, impl-drift, plan-gap, spec-gap, unforeseen} with verbatim evidence. Read-only — produces JSON; orchestrator routes. (Tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash)
- dp-qg-bugtrace: Bugfix root-cause analyzer. For each [FIX] / fix(...) commit, uses git blame to find the introducing commit, reads the originating feature's spec/plan/retro and the LEARNED-RULES that were active at that time, and classifies root cause across 6 categories (spec-gap, plan-gap, impl-drift, rule-induced, rule-missed, unforeseen). Proposes feedback to learn / history / gate-tuning. Read-only — produces proposals; user approves. (Tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash)
- dp-qg-history: Rule-health auditor. Mines auto-fixes logs + retrospectives + LEARNED-RULES-detailed.md to compute per-rule health metrics (triggers, accepts, rejects, retries, citations) and proposes deprecate / revise / merge actions for unhealthy or stale rules. Runs in light mode every pre-merge and in deep mode when rework-event anomaly detected or user-invoked. Read-only — produces proposals for user approval. (Tools: Read, Grep, Glob)
- dp-qg-impl-audit: Per-phase implementation auditor. Given the requirements and plan IRs and the git diff of a phase, emits a read-only findings report covering three probes: coverage (spec clauses not implemented), creep (code implementing nothing in spec), and compliance (CLAUDE.md / principles / standards / learned-rules violations). MUST quote exact spec clauses; NEVER paraphrase. Produces machine-parseable JSON for the orchestrator to apply patches. (Tools: Read, Grep, Glob, LSP, Bash)
- dp-qg-learn: Learning loop agent. Mines retrospectives + auto-fixes log + review reports to propose concrete rule diffs. Writes synchronized pairs to LEARNED-RULES.md (condensed LLM-loaded table row) and LEARNED-RULES-detailed.md (human-readable full section). Each proposal is dedup-checked against existing rules, verified for non-conflict with canonical rules, and presented to the user for per-rule approve/reject. Read-only until orchestrator applies. (Tools: Read, Grep, Glob)
- dp-qg-plan-audit: Post-tasks plan validator. Independently cross-checks the requirements and plan IRs for bidirectional coverage (every FR has a plan step and vice versa), TS feasibility (every referenced module/component/store exists or is in scope), projected layer/SRP violations per UI.md component architecture, hidden dependencies, and internal contradictions. Uses LSP to verify TS symbols. Read-only; emits JSON findings (QgFindingsDocument). (Tools: Read, Grep, Glob, LSP)
- dp-qg-spec-audit: Post-clarify spec auditor. Given the user's original request, the requirements IR, and the spec-phase decisions.md ledger sibling (when provided), detects missing requirements, ambiguous clauses, hidden TS/React/PWA/Electron assumptions, and out-of-scope additions. Read-only; emits JSON findings (QgFindingsDocument) for the orchestrator. Loads project snapshot to avoid flagging valid project patterns as ambiguity. (Tools: Read, Grep, Glob)
- dp-runner-judge: Opus quality judge for agentic-code-runner output ONLY. Given a task requirement + the local model's produced diff (and optional runner telemetry), returns a structured accept/reject verdict with runner-defect classification and attribution, for the runner-improvement backlog. Read-only — never modifies code, never fixes the task. MUST NOT be used to review normal Claude subagent/skill output — it exists solely to gate locally-generated runner implementations. (Tools: Bash, Read, Glob, Grep)
- Explore: Read-only search agent for broad fan-out searches — when answering means sweeping many files, directories, or naming conventions and you only need the conclusion, not the file dumps. It reads excerpts rather than whole files, so it locates code; it doesn't review or audit it. Specify search breadth: "medium" for moderate exploration, "very thorough" for multiple locations and naming conventions. (Tools: All tools except Agent, Artifact, ArtifactComments, ArtifactData, ArtifactCheck, ExitPlanMode, Edit, Write, NotebookEdit)
- final-review-orchestrator: Read-only post-development review orchestrator. Executes the Pre-Merge / Final Review workflow (tests, lint, type-check, build, snapshot drift, deps, architectural review, code review, dp-qg-impl-audit, dp-qg-bugtrace, dp-qg-history light), spawns nested reviewer subagents, writes a consolidated report file, and returns a compact summary to the caller. MUST NOT perform any git operations, PR operations, auto-refactor, or auto-fix. (Tools: Bash, Read, Glob, Grep, Write, Agent)
- general-purpose: General-purpose agent for researching complex questions, searching for code, and executing multi-step tasks. When you are searching for a keyword or file and are not confident that you will find the right match in the first few tries use this agent to perform the search for you. (Tools: *)
- haiku-coverage-checker: Verifiable coverage extractor. Given a list of IDs (FRs or I-NNs) and a diff or set of files, finds evidence for each ID and emits structured JSON with file:line citations. Every citation MUST be grep-verifiable. Output is validated post-hoc by tools/scripts/verify-coverage-citations.ts. (Tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash)
- Plan: Software architect agent for designing implementation plans. Use this when you need to plan the implementation strategy for a task. Returns step-by-step plans, identifies critical files, and considers architectural trade-offs. (Tools: All tools except Agent, Artifact, ArtifactComments, ArtifactData, ArtifactCheck, ExitPlanMode, Edit, Write, NotebookEdit)
- retrospective-analyzer: Analyzes phase retrospectives and Pre-Merge results to produce FINAL-SUMMARY. Reads phase retro files + pre-merge scratch log, applies prioritization weights, finds cross-phase patterns, and writes a comprehensive implementation summary. Does NOT write application code or tests. (Tools: Read, Write, Glob, Grep)
- skill-auditor: Expert skill auditor for Claude Code Skills. Use when auditing, reviewing, or evaluating SKILL.md files for best practices compliance. MUST BE USED when user asks to audit a skill. (Tools: Read, Grep, Glob)
- slash-command-auditor: Expert slash command auditor for Claude Code slash commands. Use when auditing, reviewing, or evaluating slash command .md files for best practices compliance. MUST BE USED when user asks to audit a slash command. (Tools: Read, Grep, Glob)
- snapshot-generator: Regenerate the project snapshot programmatically. Thin wrapper around the architectural-snapshot-create command for automated invocation (e.g., Pre-Merge workflow step 19). (Tools: Bash, Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep, LSP)
- statusline-setup: Use this agent to configure the user's Claude Code status line setting. (Tools: Read, Edit)
- subagent-auditor: Expert subagent auditor for Claude Code subagents. Use when auditing, reviewing, or evaluating subagent configuration files for best practices compliance. MUST BE USED when user asks to audit a subagent. (Tools: Read, Grep, Glob)
- text-webfetch: Playwright-based web page content extractor, web fetcher. Fetches one or more URLs using Playwright, extracts main content via Readability, converts to structured GitHub-Flavored Markdown (preserving headings, code blocks, tables, lists), and persists LLM-optimized output. Use when you need to fetch and read web pages for research. (Tools: Bash, Read, Write, Glob)
- tools-code-logic-writer: Expert TypeScript writer for the repository's own tooling under `tools/` — the agentic-code-runner and its verdict-service, the speckit-orchestrator, task-dag, deterministic scripts, and shared libraries. Owns BOTH the failing test and the implementation in one run (red→green). Does NOT touch `src/` (use code-logic-writer) and writes no UI. (Tools: Bash, Write, Edit, Glob, Read, Grep, LSP)
- ts-test-runner: Expert TS/JS npm test runner that executes test suites and returns only actionable failure information. Use when you need to run tests and get token-efficient results for debugging decisions. Accepts a test command as input. Filters noise like passing tests, expected errors in negative test cases, and irrelevant stack frames. Does NOT modify code or fix failures - use a debugger subagent for fixes after reviewing results. (Tools: Bash)

